cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this code, please cite both the original work by Di Carlo
  (on which this is based) and this repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# CITATION 1: Original method and base code by Di Carlo
# This repository is an extension of:
# https://github.com/lucadic/IsingCG
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Di Carlo
        given-names: Luca
    title: >
      Coarse-graining the Ising model with the inverse Ising problem
    year: 2024
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.04811
    repository-code: https://github.com/lucadic/IsingCG
    notes: >
      The base Monte Carlo sampling, Kadanoff blocking, and
      pseudo-likelihood inference code is taken from this work.
      The present repository extends it by adding Z2-odd operators
      (magnetic field h and three-spin coupling h3) to both the
      forward simulation and the inverse inference.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# CITATION 2: This repository (master's thesis extension)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
title: >
  ising_odd_RG_flow: Tracking Z2-odd operators under RG flow
  in the 2D Ising model
authors:
  - family-names: Granados
    given-names: Juana
    # add your ORCID here if you have one:
    # orcid: https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025
repository-code: https://github.com/juanagranadosr/ising_odd_RG_flow
abstract: >
  Extension of Di Carlo's IsingCG repository to include Z2-odd
  operators (magnetic field h and three-spin coupling h3) in both
  the Monte Carlo forward simulation and the pseudo-likelihood
  inverse Ising inference. Used to numerically study symmetry
  protection of odd operators under Kadanoff block-spin
  renormalization group flow. Developed as part of a master's
  thesis on the hierarchy problem and GOOFY symmetries.
keywords:
  - Ising model
  - renormalization group
  - symmetry protection
  - inverse Ising
  - pseudo-likelihood
  - JAX
  - Monte Carlo
  - hierarchy problem
license: MIT
